{
  "description": "Controlled vocabulary of pre-1666 London parishes from MarineLives Semantic MediaWiki, with geo-coordinates from Wikipedia. 112 parishes total. Used to normalise parish names extracted from HCA deposition front matter and for future geospatial mapping.",
  "source": "https://www.marinelives.org/wiki/Category:Semantic_parish",
  "last_updated": "2026-04-26",
  "version": "1.1",
  "version_history": [
    {"version": "1.0", "date": "2026-04-22", "context": "Initial creation from MarineLives data, but file in skill folder and Customize was truncated at 19,679 bytes mid-Saint Thomas the Apostle entry."},
    {"version": "1.1", "date": "2026-04-26", "context": "Reconstructed from authoritative MarineLives source (https://www.marinelives.org/wiki/Category:Semantic_parish, 112 pages). Completed Saint Thomas the Apostle entry (with coordinates). Added Saint Vedast Foster Lane and Stepney that were missing from v1.0. Closed JSON properly."}
  ],
  "usage": "Match the raw place extracted from front matter against the normalised_name field (case-insensitive). Handle St/Saint variation: 'St Dunstans' should match 'Saint Dunstans in the East', 'St.' should match 'Saint'. Handle Allhallows/All Hallows variation. Use partial matching as a fallback — if the raw place contains a parish name or vice versa, flag as a partial match for human review. Places outside the City of London (Wapping, Deptford, Limehouse, Shadwell, foreign ports) are expected to be UNMATCHED unless the deponent's hamlet implies a known parish (in which case use place-imputation.json's hamlet_to_parish lookup) — this is a feature, not a bug, as it distinguishes City-dwellers from others. The ambiguous 'Saint Mary Magdalen' (no qualifier) could be Bermondsey, Milk Street, or Old Fish Street — flag for human disambiguation. Coordinates are for downstream geospatial use, not for matching.",
  "notes": "WORK IN PROGRESS. Coordinates are in DMS format from Wikipedia. The list includes City of London parishes, some Southwark parishes (Saint Olave Southwark, Saint Saviour Southwark, Saint Thomas Southwark, Saint George the Martyr Southwark, Saint Marie Overie), and Stepney (which covered Wapping, Limehouse, Ratcliffe, Shadwell, Poplar, Blackwall as hamlets). Not all parishes have complete coordinate data. 'Saint Mary Magdalen' without qualifier appears in the list — context determines whether this is Bermondsey or another dedication.",
